SUMMARY:The State of Tech & AI Jobs\, panel discussion & onsite Jobs Board
DESCRIPTION:All Things Open RTP Meetup\nThe August meetup will be a doozie
 !\n\nOne year ago our meetup focused on The State of Jobs in tech and open
  source and the impact of AI - and interest was through the roof. This mon
 th\, we'll revisit the same topic one year later as things continue to cha
 nge and evolve rapidly.\n\nProgramming will include **a State of IT Jobs 1
 5-minute talk** from Taylor Desseyn\, VP of Global Community @ Randstad Di
 gital/Torc\, **a panel discussion featuring Hiring Managers and Jobs exper
 ts**\, as well as **an onsite Jobs Board with active\, open jobs**.\n\nThe
  meetup is free to attend\, but an RSVP is required. Networking\, swag (sh
 irts\, hats and stickers) will be plentiful\, and (limited) food and bever
 ages will be available.\n\nDoors open at 6:00 pm\, live programming kicks 
 off at 6:30 sharp.\nWe'll be back at The Barn at Bandwidth's RTP campus. I
 t's a world-class venue and it's one our community LOVES visiting!\n\nLoca
 tion:\nThe Barn at Bandwidth Raleigh office\n2230 Bandmate Way\nRaleigh\, 
 NC 27607\n**[Additional Venue Details](https://www.bandwidth.com/bandmate-
 way/)**\, including parking\n*\\*note\, additional visitor parking will be
  available onsite on the 27th*\n\n**Questions?** Contact us at [info@allth
 ingsopen.org.](http://info@allthingsopen.org./)\n\n**Made Possible By Rand
 stad Digital powered by Torc**\nThis meetup is in partnership with and mad
 e possible by the team at Randstad Digital powered by Torc.\n\nRandstad Di
 gital powered by Torc is a global community for technology professionals l
 ooking to grow their careers\, meet good people\, build new skills\, and s
 tay connected to opportunities along the way.\n\n* [Check out the website 
 here](https://www.torc.dev/community-ato?utm_source=atonewsletter&utm_medi
 um=email&utm_campaign=atopartnership)\n* [Discord ](torc.dev/discord)\n* [
 LinkedIn ](https://www.linkedin.com/company/torcdotdev/)\n* Social handle 
 (all platforms) - @torcdotdev\n* Community Email - [community@torc.dev](ma
 ilto:community@torc.dev "mailto:community@torc.dev")\n* Primary contact - 
 Taylor\, VP of Global Community\n* Additional team contact - Briana\, Head
  of Global Operations\n\n**RSVP required**\n\\*This is a free event. Howev
 er\, an RSVP is required. Seating is limited\, so RSVP's will be capped as
  we fill up. Please move quickly and RSVP to save your spot if interested.
  When you RSVP you will be added to our mailing list to receive future eve
 nt updates. You can unsubscribe at any time.
